# S11-R-02 dynamic probe: force a `large_radius_event` termination on an
# EXPANDING shell and read back `isCollapse`.
#
# Same physical setup as harness/phase6_short.param (mCloud 1e5 Msun, sfe 0.3,
# homogeneous densPL_alpha=0 -> rCloud = 1.6900 pc, coll_r = 1.0 pc), with the
# single change that `stop_r` is lowered from the schema default 500 pc to 3 pc.
#
# Why 3 pc: `max_radius` is only built into the 1b / 1c / 2 event lists, never
# phase 1a/1 (`build_energy_phase_events` = cloud_boundary, min_radius,
# velocity_runaway). The shell must therefore leave the cloud at rCloud = 1.69 pc
# and cross stop_r afterwards. 3 pc sits above rCloud, so the event gets a real
# upward crossing (direction=+1) in phase 1b instead of starting already past it.
#
# Expected physical fate: the shell is EXPANDING outward through 3 pc.
# SimulationEndCode = LARGE_RADIUS (2) -- a clean, successful termination.
# `isCollapse` must therefore be False.
mCloud    1e5
sfe    0.3
stop_t    0.5
stop_r    3.0
